			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				765,
				160
			],
			"Message": "style(Land): Apply consistent formatting with blank-line separators across build pipeline and polyfills\n\nStandardize the build pipeline and polyfill source files by inserting blank lines between logical blocks and import statements. This formatting pass applies to the Output pipeline, ESBuild configurations, plugin definitions, polyfills, and service implementations under Land/Element/Output.\n\nThe changes introduce visual separation between import declarations, variable bindings, function definitions, and control-flow blocks throughout 150+ source files. No functional behavior is altered; only whitespace formatting is adjusted to improve readability and maintain consistency with the project's coding conventions.",
			"SHA": "794bd357f2a1dfa84f6d9d813896877e6e6524fa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T12:49:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				765,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Refactor drag and maximize commands to use typed window API\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "50f88d74a0a3bd374dfee91b10cc5532c1e276a9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T18:18:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				765,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Use typed window API for drag/maximize with explicit label\n\nThe generic `InvokeWindowCommand(command:string)` dispatched bare `core.invoke` calls without the window `label` payload. Tauri 2.x's IPC dispatcher silently drops `plugin:window|start_dragging` invocations when no window label is provided and no window matches the implicit context — the overlay-titlebar window never moved. The typed JS API (`Window.startDragging()`, `Window.toggleMaximize()`) transparently injects the correct label from the caller's window handle.\n\nSplit `InvokeWindowCommand` into `StartDragging` and `ToggleMaximize`, each preferring the typed window API first, then falling back to raw `invoke` with an explicit `{ label }` payload. The label is resolved from `getCurrentWindow().label`, `getCurrentWebviewWindow().label`, or the literal `\"main\"` as last resort.\n\nBoth drag-initiation and titlebar double-click maximize now work reliably under Tauri 2.",
			"SHA": "79a2a5f8b62f91f4c725b13521911fa62e697e61"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1780160076460
}